prompts.attack:
Use case: identity-preserve. Production transparent sprite sheet extending the EXACT Grimhald character in reference 1. Create FOUR complete connected full-body attack animation drawings in a 2x2 equal-cell sheet, right-facing three-quarter game camera. No character redesign. Match reference's pale grey steel highlights, charcoal plates, crimson cloth, orange visor, crown helmet, slim waist, limb lengths and neutral lighting EXACTLY. Reference character is 39 logical pixels from helmet tip to soles; retain that proportion, with ample transparent padding in each cell and identical camera scale.
The weapon is a SEPARATE accessory added later: draw NO axe, shaft, sword, trails or effects. His right fist/gauntlet makes a heavy one-handed overhead-to-forward-downward strike that also reads as an unarmed hammerfist when no weapon is attached. Whole shoulders, torso, hips, knees and feet participate fluidly:
1 top-left: upright ready stance, right closed fist near shoulder, left fist near belt, both feet planted;
2 top-right: windup with the right fist above/behind the helmet, slight body twist, bent knees;
3 bottom-left: forward/downward impact, right fist extended forward around waist/chest height, weight over front leg;
4 bottom-right: follow-through and return toward shoulder-ready stance.
The grip fist must remain clearly visible so a separate wooden haft can be aligned to it. Full continuous body, not upper/lower cutouts. Same armour construction and shading in every frame, neither darker nor larger than reference. Keep all feet on the same cell baseline. Simple readable blocky art, no texture noise or light bloom. Transparent background, no floor shadow, text, grids, duplicates or cropping.
